  "verbalization": "Excisusin C is shown to have a target relationship with VMRC-LCP, which is a complex molecule with a unique structural profile. This molecule is identified as a target of multiple isomers of Excisusin C, including (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol and (1R,2R,4S,7Z,11R)-4,8-dimethyl-12-methylidene-3,14-dioxatricyclo[9.3.0.02,4]tetradec-7-en-13-one, all of which share a common target of H9. The evidence suggests that Excisusin C may act through a mechanism that involves the interaction with VMRC-LCP, which is a key player in the biological pathway leading to H9's activation. The structural diversity of Excisusin C's targets implies that the molecule may exert its effects through multiple pathways, potentially involving different molecular interactions with VMRC-LCP. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Excisusin C may influence H9 through a complex, multi-step mechanism involving VMRC-LCP, which remains a central node in the observed network.",
